{
	"about": "The globals the runtime gives a program, as a browser and WinterCG runtimes have them (and Node's own, as Bun has them: process, Buffer, global): each provider file, the globals it exports, and what the platform must be able to do for it (needs: clock, http, intl, async). A program gets only the globals it names. Read by the native linker (compiler/modules.js) and the WASI bundler (wasi/scripts/bundle.mjs); a native build with the runtime can do everything, a WASI world what it imports. A provider's `select` names the selector values it serves (selectors: where each is passed); a value the program passes brings its provider, a value the compiler cannot see brings every provider of that selector (compiler/selectors.js). A provider's `load` pattern, when the program's text matches it, loads the provider for what it does on loading.",
